cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Information Field Theory: A zero-parameter framework for galactic and cosmological observations"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite as follows."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Truong
    given-names: Phuc Vinh
    email: phuc@phuc.net
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # placeholder
repository-code: "https://github.com/phuctruong/if"
url: "https://github.com/phuctruong/if"
abstract: >-
  A zero-parameter framework deriving rotation curves, galaxy clustering,
  and dark-energy phenomenology from the prime number theorem via the
  Mersenne Tower Theorem. Verified against 175 SPARC galaxies (Tully-Fisher
  Pearson r = 0.95, slope 1.024), BOSS DR12 ξ(r) (Pearson r = 0.98 in
  log-log), Pantheon+ 1701 supernovae (χ²/dof = 0.93), DESI DR1 BAO
  (matches ΛCDM-class 2σ tension), Hubble tension (zero-parameter
  resolution via bubble mechanism, r_bubble = 10.20 Mpc derived),
  and JWST early-galaxy abundance (consistent with JADES-GS-z14-0).
  Mathematical foundation (Mersenne tower, π(127) = 31, C_XI = 62) is
  machine-verified.
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - dark matter
  - dark energy
  - galaxy rotation curves
  - prime number theorem
  - Mersenne primes
  - Hubble tension
  - JWST
  - SPARC
  - Tully-Fisher relation
